// REJECTS: Unexpected token '<EOF>'. Valid alternatives: [',', ']']
//
// An `EqualTo #{ ... }` island closed with a plain `}` instead of `}#`. Unlike
// unterminated-embedded-data.pure the delimiter is NOT missing -- there is a closing brace,
// in the right place, and it is the wrong one.
//
// This is the case a scan-to-matching-brace implementation gets wrong in the most damaging
// direction: it reads the island as complete, consumes the rest of the enclosing element as
// if it were service body, and either succeeds with truncated content or fails somewhere
// unrelated. legend-engine's island lexer stays in island mode and runs to end of input.
###Service
Service fixture::neg::IslandClosedWithBrace
{
   pattern: '/x';
   documentation: 'd';
   execution: Single
   {
      query: |fixture::neg::Person.all();
      mapping: fixture::neg::M;
      runtime: fixture::neg::R;
   }
   testSuites:
   [
      suite1:
      {
         tests:
         [
            t1:
            {
               asserts:
               [
                  a1:
                     EqualTo
                     #{
                        expected: '1';
                     }
               ]
            }
         ]
      }
   ]
}
